# Cloudflare Pages headers for the nessa project (hub site + /thriftlux catalog).
#
# The ThriftLux admin lives at /thriftlux/admin. By default CF Pages sends no
# Cache-Control on HTML, so browsers — especially the WhatsApp/Instagram in-app
# webviews owners use — heuristically cache a stale admin.html for hours. After a
# redeploy the owner then sees an old admin (missing newly-added sections) until
# that cache expires. `no-cache` forces a revalidation on every load (304 when
# unchanged, fresh when redeployed) so admin changes show up immediately.
# Versioned assets (admin.js?v=, styles.css?v=) keep their long cache.
/thriftlux/admin
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
/thriftlux/admin.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
